# Advanced Search feature wiring

When adding **editor toolbar actions**, **page-specific actions** (print, etc.), or **Settings toggle switches**, also expose them in Advanced Search in the same change. Do not ship UI-only controls without an AS entry.

## Where to register

| Kind | Module | Pattern |
|------|--------|---------|
| Markdown editor toolbar (bold, AI, …) | `src/utils/advancedSearch/editorActions.ts` | Add `EditorActionId` + `EDITOR_ACTION_COMMANDS`; register handler in `MarkdownEditor.jsx` via `registerEditorActions` |
| Print / export-pdf page | `src/utils/advancedSearch/printActions.ts` | Add `PrintActionId` + `PRINT_ACTION_COMMANDS` (or paper cmds); register in `ExportPDFPage.jsx` via `registerPrintActions` / TOC provider |
| Chat page (composer focus, …) | `src/utils/advancedSearch/chatActions.ts` | Add `ChatActionId` + `CHAT_ACTION_COMMANDS`; register in `ChatComposer.jsx` via `registerChatActions` |
| Settings toggle (켜기/끄기) | `src/utils/advancedSearch/settingsToggles.ts` | Add `SettingsToggleId` + def in `SETTINGS_TOGGLE_DEFS` (`load`/`save`, situational enable/disable titles); sync UI via `subscribeSettingsToggles` / `setSettingsToggle` |
| Nested picker / browse mode | `openRequest.ts` mode + `AdvancedSearchHost.tsx` | Like `print-paper` / `browse-directory` / `chat-groups`: keep modal open when drilling in; browse mode includes `browse-new-file` / `browse-new-folder` → `onRequestCreateItem` |
| Chat group selection | `chatGroups.ts` + Host `getChatGroups` | Command `chat-select-group` → nested list; select navigates `/chat#group-{id}` |

Commands are ranked in `commands.ts` (`matchAppCommandsRanked` / `scoreCommandRelevance`). Page toolbar + settings toggles appear on **non-empty queries** (relevance-filtered). Empty palette stays core app shortcuts only unless you intentionally add a core `APP_COMMANDS` entry.

## Checklist for every new control

1. **Id + labels + keywords** (KO/EN) in the right module above.
2. **Handler** registered while the page/editor is mounted (or `load`/`save` for toggles).
3. **Host** (`AdvancedSearchHost.tsx`): handle select if not covered by `editor-*` / `print-*` / `isSettingsToggleId` prefixes.
4. **Situational copy** for toggles: show only **켜기** or **끄기** from current state (never both).
5. Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.

```text
❌ BAD — Settings Switch only in SettingsPage, no AS command
❌ BAD — Toolbar button with no EDITOR_ACTION_COMMANDS entry
✅ GOOD — Toggle in settingsToggles.ts + Settings UI calls setSettingsToggle
✅ GOOD — New MdEditor toolbar action registered in editorActions + MarkdownEditor
```
